0008319E                          2734  * after the value is evaluated a test is made on the next BASIC program byte, if it
0008319E                          2735  * is a comparrison operator i.e. "<", "=" or ">", then the corresponding bit is set
0008319E                          2736  * in the comparison evaluation flag. this test loops until no more comparrison operators
0008319E                          2737  * are found or more than one of any type is found. in the last case an error is generated
