00084872                          6959  *************************************************************************************
00084872                          6960  *
00084872                          6961  * RND(n), 32 bit Galois version. make n=0 for 19th next number in sequence or n<>0
00084872                          6962  * to get 19th next number in sequence after seed n. This version of the PRNG uses
00084872                          6963  * the Galois method and a sample of 65536 bytes produced gives the following values.
00084872                          6964  
00084872                          6965  * Entropy = 7.997442 bits per byte
00084872                          6966  * Optimum compression would reduce these 65536 bytes by 0 percent
00084872                          6967  
00084872                          6968  * Chi square distribution for 65536 samples is 232.01, and
00084872                          6969  * randomly would exceed this value 75.00 percent of the time
00084872                          6970  
00084872                          6971  * Arithmetic mean value of data bytes is 127.6724, 127.5 would be random
00084872                          6972  * Monte Carlo value for Pi is 3.122871269, error 0.60 percent
00084872                          6973  * Serial correlation coefficient is -0.000370, totally uncorrelated would be 0.0
00084872                          6974  
00084872                          6975  LAB_RND
